{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.99,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U11", "Q9"],
      "pins": ["U10.4", "U10.5", "U10.8", "U11.4", "U11.5", "U11.8", "Q9.2", "Q9.3"],
      "nets": ["GND", "5V_switched_CAN", "+5V"],
      "observed": "Both isolated CAN transceivers have GND1 and GND2 tied to the same GND net. Their VCC2 pins are powered from 5V_switched_CAN, which is switched from the board's +5V rail by Q9; no separate isolated supply domain is shown.",
      "expected": "To provide the specified isolated CAN interfaces, the transceiver-side ground and supply must remain galvanically isolated from the logic-side ground and supply. GND1 and GND2 should not be joined, and VCC2 needs an isolated supply.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1) ... through an isolated CAN transceiver (U11/companion)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"80\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") ...)(node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") ...)(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") ...)(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"52\") (name \"5V_switched_CAN\") ... (node (ref \"Q9\") (pin \"3\") ...)(node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC2\") ...)(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC2\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"Q9\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\") ...))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN interfaces do not provide galvanic isolation as specified. Ground-potential differences or transients on the external CAN wiring can couple into the board's logic ground and electronics.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is present: both CAN transceivers are identified as isolated, but their logic-side and bus-side grounds are joined, and their bus-side supplies derive from the ordinary +5V rail. This defeats the specified galvanic isolation."
}

